fastmark — a fast drop-in for marked 18.1.3 (MIT, see LICENSE)

parse.js is a fork of marked 18.1.3, rewritten as a single dependency-free
ES module with marked's default options baked in (GFM on, breaks off,
pedantic off, async off). It renders exactly the HTML that marked 18.1.3's
marked.parse(markdown) returns with those defaults, on every input.

  upstream    marked@18.1.3 on npm (published 2026-11-02)
  source      https://github.com/markedjs/marked, tag v18.1.3,
              commit ba50aa95636ac8f97f46446bbfeb04592ed22216
  licence     MIT (Copyright (c) 2018+, MarkedJS;
              Copyright (c) 2011-2018, Christopher Jeffrey); LICENSE also
              carries the original Markdown's BSD-style notice
              (Copyright 2004, John Gruber)

What changed from upstream (behaviour-preserving under the defaults):
  - the Marked wrapper class, options merging, extensions, hooks and
    walkTokens are gone; parse() drives the Lexer and Parser directly
  - only the GFM block/inline grammars are built; pedantic and
    breaks variants are not included
  - hot paths dispatch on the first character instead of trying every
    tokenizer regex in turn, and a few allocations were removed

Everything else — the regexes, the tokenizer, the lexer state machine and
the renderer — follows upstream exactly, so the output is byte-for-byte
identical to marked 18.1.3 with default options.
